nio: give the USB gadget 20 minutes before the automatic reset

Run 651 brought up the DWC3 USB gadget, but the 150 s PSCI auto-reset
fires before the host can enumerate it, photograph the panel, or (once
live-log lands) stream a console.  The reset is a cold boot, so the
ramoops console is lost with it.

Keep the automatic reset -- it is what returns the phone to rooted
Android without a power-key press -- but move it out to 20 minutes so
the gadget has time to enumerate and the owner can read the panel.  A
boot-arg overrides it when a shorter cycle is wanted.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -530,4 +530,8 @@ nio_auto_reboot_thread(void *arg, wait_result_t wr)
 {
-#define NIO_AUTO_REBOOT_NS 150000000000ULL   /* 150 seconds */
+	/* nio: 150 s was too short -- the USB gadget needs time to enumerate
+	 * and the panel needs to be readable before the cold reset. */
+	int nio_reboot_secs = 1200;
+	PE_parse_boot_argn("nioreboot", &nio_reboot_secs, sizeof(nio_reboot_secs));
+#define NIO_AUTO_REBOOT_NS ((uint64_t)nio_reboot_secs * 1000000000ULL)
 	uint64_t start_ns = 0, now_ns = 0;
 	clock_get_uptime(&start_ns);
